# flickos-screenshot: the Print keys, Super+Shift+S and Super+Shift+R (bar
# --video, since 1.1) run it. A Depends, not a Recommends like the other keys'
# programs, because they worked before it existed: this keeps
# flickos-settings back until it can be installed too.
         flickos-screenshot (>= 1.1),
         ${misc:Depends}
# autostart leaves starting mako to flickos-layout panel (flickos-layouts 1.3),
# runs flickos-layout first-run (1.4) and flickos-layout wallpaper (1.6).
# It runs flickos-control night-light and notifications (1.8), startup run
# (1.9) and lock (1.10, the lock script) when flickos-control is installed;
# an older one would leave night light off or the screen unlocked. The
# menu's Displays runs flickos-control displays arrange (1.21).
# Super+Shift+D runs flick-tiler show-desktop (1.7).
# The zoom keys send flickos-shortcuts SIGWINCH so its sheet stays away while
# Super is held for them, and it names them (1.14); flickos-session's
# labwc -m needs a sheet that reads the merged files (1.16).
Breaks: flickos-layouts (<< 1.6),
        flickos-control (<< 1.21),
        flick-tiler (<< 1.7),
        flickos-shortcuts (<< 1.16)
# Recommends: programs used by keybindings and menu entries.
